United States","Global Modern Slavery Training rolled out to all employees to ensure that risks are understood, red flags can be spotted and the reporting is safe and robust within a process that is victim led at all times.  
We have strong DEI programmes and ensure inclusitivity across all areas of our direct business where everyone has value. 
Our charity work across the group supports our demographic within retail and our communities in which we operate.  https://www.neighbourly.com/jdfoundation","Goods Not for Resale (GNFR) 

These workers include cleaning, logistics & catering within our operations, is high risk.  We work with UnSeen to ensure risks are identified across our peer groups.",Within your own operations,,"Women
Migrants
Other vulnerable groups","Ethnic minorities , Disabled",United Kingdom,"Workers within these sectors may be at increased risk of modern slavery due to factors such as low-paid & temporary employment, the use of labour agencies, migrant labour, subcontracting arrangements and limited visibility beyond  first tier of the supply chain. Through the Procurement Team we upload all of the contractors to the UnSeen webstie and collaborate with other businesses on issues which are reported on the platform, operating a combined approach to resolution with the relevent company","Abuse of vulnerability
