United Kingdom","TWFRS requires suppliers to comply with the Modern Slavery Act 2015 through procurement and tender processes. Mandatory and discretionary exclusion grounds are applied where modern slavery concerns exist. Suppliers are expected to take appropriate steps to manage risks within their own supply chains. Procurement activity is undertaken in accordance with the Authority's Financial and Procurement Regulations and ethical procurement standards, including CIPS Corporate Ethics Register requirements","Temporary, agency and contract workers engaged by suppliers and contractors who may be vulnerable to labour exploitation or unethical recruitment practices.",Within your supply chains,"Tier 1 suppliers
Tier 2 suppliers
Tier 3 suppliers and below","Migrants
Other vulnerable groups","Temporary, agency and contract workers recruited through third-party labour providers.",United Kingdom,TWFRS undertakes due diligence when engaging suppliers and contractors to identify risks of forced labour and unethical recruitment practices. Suppliers are required to comply with the Modern Slavery Act 2015 and are expected to take appropriate steps to manage risks within their own workforce and supply chains. Procurement processes include supplier checks and exclusion measures where modern slavery concerns are identified.,"Individuals recruited through third-party agencies who may be vulnerable to coercion, forced labour, human trafficking or other forms of exploitation.",Within your own operations,,"Migrants
Other vulnerable groups","Individuals recruited through third-party employment agencies, including temporary and agency workers.",United Kingdom,"TWFRS undertakes robust pre-employment checks, including verification of right to work, references, criminal record checks and occupational health screening where appropriate. Due diligence is undertaken when engaging third-party agencies and suppliers to identify risks of forced labour, modern slavery and unethical recruitment practices. Staff receive safeguarding and modern slavery training and concerns can be reported through safeguarding and whistleblowing processes.",,Yes,,,"Progress is demonstrated through quarterly review of modern slavery KPIs, 98% staff completion of mandatory modern slavery training, 98% staff confidence in identifying concerns, ongoing supplier due diligence, and regular review of policies and procedures.",2026-07-30T13:26:00,https://downloads.modern-slavery-statement-registry.service.gov.uk/pdf-published/EGf7dz2o/2026/Modern Slavery Statement 2025-2026 - with signatures.pdf
