Migrants",,China,"We manage modern slavery risk in PPE, workwear and branded uniform supply chains through two framework agreements. Monthly supplier reviews include a risk matrix, checks that key suppliers maintain ethical and anti-slavery statements, and assessment of any risks affecting workers involved in manufacturing and distribution. Identified risks are categorised, investigated and managed through agreed mitigation and monitoring actions across relevant supply chain locations.","Waste management and recycling operations across UK sites rely on complex supply chains. Temporary, agency and lower-skilled workers are at higher risk due to multiple service providers.",Within your supply chains,Tier 1 suppliers,"Migrants
Refugees",,United Kingdom,"All our tenders for waste management requirements (inclusive 
of hazardous waste, chemical cleans, grits, screenings and 
general waste collections) have been tendered over the last 12 
months. Within each tender, questions on modern slavery are included 
building on lessons learned from previous tenders and 
updated to adhere to the latest policy and market risks.","Field operatives and contractor crews deliver network maintenance, repairs and capital works across the UU region. Risks arise from subcontractors, off-framework spend and limited oversight.",Within your supply chains,Tier 1 suppliers,"Women
Migrants
Refugees
Children",,"China
United Kingdom
India","We have strengthened oversight of our chemical supply chain through enhanced due diligence, including supplier site visits to assess working conditions and employment practices. We continue to work with industry partners through established water sector forums to address modern slavery risks collectively, share intelligence, and identify opportunities for a coordinated approach to improving supply chain transparency and worker protections.",,Yes,,,"Our 2026 Statement demonstrates progress through the introduction of a Supplier Code of Conduct, development of modern slavery audit standards with Slave-Free Alliance, and increased awareness training, achieving 97% completion in relevant community-based roles. We also set measurable future goals, including achieving 95% responsible sourcing compliance and auditing 10% of suppliers by 2030, enabling us to track and demonstrate continued improvement.",2026-09-04T06:27:30,https://downloads.modern-slavery-statement-registry.service.gov.uk/pdf-published/C1u3suql/2026/anti-slavery-and-human-trafficking-statement-2026.pdf
