Tier 3 suppliers and below",,,,"The University uses supplier due diligence questionnaires for contracts over £125,000 and recommends them for £25,000 to £125,000 contracts. Preferred suppliers are reviewed at least annually, asked to confirm Modern Slavery Act compliance and provide policy statements, and review templates flag high-risk goods and services to prompt supplier discussions on onward supply chains.","Modern slavery risks linked to outsourced labour, including security, cleaning and housekeeping services, within centrally managed spend.",Within your supply chains,Tier 1 suppliers,,,,"The University maintains Living Wage and Oxford Living Wage accreditation covering employees and contractor/subcontractor staff working regularly on University premises in the UK. Supplier due diligence and annual preferred supplier reviews seek Modern Slavery Act confirmations, policy statements and details of actions taken to combat modern slavery.","Employment-related risks in activities conducted outside central University operations and oversight, including temporary staffing and overseas work.",Within your own operations,,,,,"The University completes appropriate pre-employment checks, provides recruitment guidance including on under-18s, uses TSS processes for temporary workers and asks external agencies to confirm equivalent checks.",,Yes,,,In the 2024/25 statement we have committed to reviewing risk assessment processes in 2025/26.,2026-08-05T13:55:49,https://downloads.modern-slavery-statement-registry.service.gov.uk/pdf-published/uEsUuqoY/2026/GPC Modern Slavery Statement 2024-25 Approved 20102025.pdf
