Through trade unions or other worker representative groups",No,"Track monthly KPIs with workforce provider related to modern slavery prevention, for example welfare checks, refresher training and key data checks.",No,"Workers categorised as ‘very likely sector risk’ are agency workers sorting recycling in our Material Recycling Facility based in London, UK",Within your own operations,,Migrants,,United Kingdom,"We work proactively and collaboratively with our principal  labour agency and require monthly reporting on modern slavery KPIs, for example: Induction processes for all employees; Welfare interviews with five  employees per quarter with a regional manager (not affiliated with the site); Right to Work document checks at least once a month and verifying bank details for five employees monthly; and Refresher training in modern slavery risks, policy, and the confidential helpline annually.",Workers sourced from small labour security providers at our sites in London,Within your own operations,,Migrants,,United Kingdom,"All suppliers are required to ensure compliance with the Modern Slavery Act 2015 and with other applicable anti-slavery and human trafficking laws, regulations and codes; and notify Cory of the awareness of any breach or potential breach of these laws, regulations and codes or any of
its anti-slavery policies. Each year, we audit a selection of suppliers in the higher risk  category, as well as undertake rolling audits of lower risk suppliers.","Providers of civil works, and  facilities management services, such as cleaning and catering to our sites in London, UK",Within your own operations,,Migrants,,United Kingdom,"All suppliers are required to ensure compliance with the Modern Slavery Act 2015 and with other applicable anti-slavery and human trafficking laws, regulations and codes; and notify Cory of the awareness of any breach or potential breach of these laws, regulations and codes or any of
its anti-slavery policies. Each year, we audit a selection of suppliers in the higher risk  category, as well as undertake rolling audits of lower risk suppliers.",,Yes,,,"We report on key achievements during the reporting period, and include targets for the following reporting period. For example, targets for 2026 include: publishing a remediation protocol summary, undertaking a business model check to ensure procurement practices do not increase supply chain risks, and auditing suppliers in industries most exposed to risk.",2026-03-30T15:16:39,https://downloads.modern-slavery-statement-registry.service.gov.uk/pdf-published/ZZEOjBA8/2026/Cory_ModernSlaveryStatement_04_02_26.pdf
