United Kingdom
India
Italy
United States","Nationwide addresses labour exploitation risks in its supply chain through supplier due diligence and risk based contractual expectations. Due diligence includes testing controls against the Third Party Code of Practice, reviewing FSQS and EcoVadis responses, and service-specific checks (eg Sedex SMETA audits on uniform factories). Corrective actions are requested and tracked where issues are identified. Nationwide promotes responsible purchasing practices through internal training and guidance.",Vulnerable customers at risk of exploitation,Within your own operations,,"Women
Migrants
Refugees
Children",,United Kingdom,"Nationwide will continue to support vulnerable customers through trauma-informed specialist teams, improved recording of support needs and accessible communication tools. We will strengthen colleague training to identify exploitation, expand safe spaces and Easy Read support, use intelligence to improve detection, and signpost customers to trusted charities, safeguarding bodies and law enforcement where needed.",,Yes,,,"The 2026 statement demonstrates progress over time through its “Our progress and ambitions” section, which summarises the actions completed during 2025/26 and sets out future ambitions. It also includes year-on-year KPIs showing how Nationwide measures improvement and tracks effectiveness over time.",2026-08-19T10:35:30,https://downloads.modern-slavery-statement-registry.service.gov.uk/pdf-published/DgEnJPVp/2026/Modern Slavery 2026 - government registry.pdf
