Through trade unions or other worker representative groups",No,Some of our largest sites are audited under the Electronics Industry's RBA programme. Our supply chain focus for audits is on labour based service contracts on our sites.,No,5 countries in which we have operations account for 91% of our global workforce. These 5 countries have been identified through our risk assessment as priority locations for our focus.,Within your own operations,,Other vulnerable groups,"Unknown, we are yet to establish specific vulnerable groups at a country by country basis.","China
Indonesia
India
Mexico
Turkey",We are implementing a site audit programme and we will report on this assessment in next year's statement,Just under half of our spend sits in countries scoring above our risk threshold. We are adjusting our supply chain risk assessment and due diligence activities to align with this risk profile.,Within your supply chains,Don't know,Other vulnerable groups,We do not have granular visibility of specific vulnerable groups within our Tier 1 supply chain and have no visibility beyond that with the exception of our smelter-level due diligence programme that forms part of our work on conflict minerals.,,"We are developing a labour, human rights and modern slavery/human trafficking audit framework with our supply chain professionals. Once in place this will strengthen the existing supplier audit programme.",Copper is our largest raw material exposure with the highest average country risk.  We align this with our smelter-level due diligence we are already perform under our conflict minerals programme.,Within your supply chains,Don't know,Other vulnerable groups,We are yet to establish a clear view of the minority groups affected by our use of Copper within the business.,,"We have a smelter-level due diligence programme underway which forms part of our work around conflict minerals.  We are expanding our focus on our copper supply chain and will report on this, in more detail, in next year's disclosures.",,Yes,,,"We have included in our statement 5 initial KPIs to enable our Board to judge our activity in reducing modern slavery risk in our business and supply chain.  These are:
1) Supplier Audit Programme, coverage and findings
2) Training of front line and key staff - completion rates
3) Speak Up Reports (whistleblowing) cases
4) Independent assurance programme coverage including RBA
5) Percentage of our workforce that is variable i.e. not on payroll, either employed via outsourcing or other agencies.",2026-09-15T06:47:03,https://downloads.modern-slavery-statement-registry.service.gov.uk/pdf-published/ZdC6ijr8/2026/Volex Modern Slavery Statement 2026 - September - Approved.pdf
