Unannounced audit",No,"Using anonymous whistleblowing services, such as a helpline or mobile phone app",No,"We joined RISE, offering education, support to women against harassment and violence. We also partnered with Pacific Links supporting the GEMS academic program and human trafficking awareness.",No,Human trafficking/forced labour,Within your supply chains,Tier 1 suppliers,Women,,Vietnam,"In 2025, we scaled up RISE Respect™ training within our operations and trained nearly 19,000 workers in India and Vietnam. We are currently on track to reach all core Tier 1 lingerie and apparel factories in Vietnam and impact 50000 workers by 2028. We partner with Pacific Links Foundation to support GEMS academic program and human trafficking awareness.",Foreign Migrant Worker abuse,Within your supply chains,Tier 1 suppliers,Migrants,,Thailand,"VS&Co has a Foreign Migrant Worker Policy to mitigate human trafficking and forced labor risks in our supply chain. In order to use a factory that employs foreign migrant workers, the sourcing team must obtain executive approval which can only be given if the factory receives positive results on a Foreign Migrant Worker Risk Assessment in accordance with the  International Labour Organization’s handbook on Combating Forced Labour . The assessments must be conducted at least annually.",,,,,,,,,Yes,,,Our ongoing commitments and plans outlining the actions we are taking to strengthen our efforts in preventing modern slavery within our supply risks are on page 7 of our Modern Slavery Statement.,2026-06-02T16:34:47,https://downloads.modern-slavery-statement-registry.service.gov.uk/pdf-published/QEZPzcoT/2026/MST.pdf
