Third party audit arranged by your organisation",No,"Using anonymous whistleblowing services, such as a helpline or mobile phone app",No,"We monitor working conditions through site inspections, supplier reviews, open communication, whistleblowing channels, and workforce data checks to ensure ethical standards are upheld.",No,"Temporary construction workers on UK project sites, particularly subcontracted labour, may face risks around working hours, pay practices, and potential exploitation in labour-intensive activities.",Within your supply chains,Tier 1 suppliers,Migrants,,United Kingdom,"We manage this risk through robust recruitment checks, verifying right-to-work, and monitoring working hours and pay. Regular site inspections, staff training, and clear reporting channels, including whistleblowing, ensure issues are identified and addressed promptly. Subcontractors are required to adhere to our ethical standards, with audits and corrective actions applied where necessary to prevent exploitation and maintain safe, fair working conditions.","Workers involved in  manufacturing construction materials in the UK supply chain may face risks linked to unsafe conditions, agency labour use, and limited visibility beyond tier-one suppliers.",Within your supply chains,Tier 1 suppliers,Migrants,,United Kingdom,"We manage this risk through robust recruitment checks, verifying right-to-work, and monitoring working hours and pay. Regular site inspections, staff training, and clear reporting channels, including whistleblowing, ensure issues are identified and addressed promptly. Subcontractors are required to adhere to our ethical standards, with audits and corrective actions applied where necessary to prevent exploitation and maintain safe, fair working conditions.","Migrant and agency workers engaged by subcontractors across UK may be at higher risk of exploitation, particularly in recruitment practices, right-to-work checks, and employment terms.",Within your supply chains,Tier 1 suppliers,Migrants,,United Kingdom,"We manage this risk through robust recruitment checks, verifying right-to-work, and monitoring working hours and pay. Regular site inspections, staff training, and clear reporting channels, including whistleblowing, ensure issues are identified and addressed promptly. Subcontractors are required to adhere to our ethical standards, with audits and corrective actions applied where necessary to prevent exploitation and maintain safe, fair working conditions.","Abuse of vulnerability
