Supporting investigations by relevant authorities",No,"We demonstrate progress by monitoring KPIs such as supplier audits, training completion, and reported concerns. In 2025/26, we aim for 100% audits of high-risk suppliers and full employee training. Regular site inspections, risk assessments, and updated policies ensure continuous improvement, embedding ethical standards and mitigating modern slavery risks across our operations and supply chains, while tracking measurable outcomes to guide future actions.",2026-04-02T11:12:48,https://downloads.modern-slavery-statement-registry.service.gov.uk/pdf-published/juEKhjgE/2026/HR-POL-035 Modern Slavery and Human Trafficking Policy Statement.pdf
