Through trade unions or other worker representative groups",No,"Ran our gap analysis with Slave Free Alliance to understand disparity in org & supply chain, re human rights, modern slavery & labour exploitation, & align with our commitment to UNGC 10 Principles.",No,Identified gaps in our processes for Modern Slavery protections both internally within the organisation and outward facing within our supply chain management processes.,Within your supply chains,"Tier 1 suppliers
Tier 2 suppliers
Tier 3 suppliers and below","Women
Migrants
Refugees",,United Kingdom,"This year we advanced our partnership with the Slave Free Alliance by completing a baseline gap analysis, which covered internal and external aspects of modern slavery, human rights and force labour by conducting interviews with internal employees at all levels and reviewing all our policies and procedure documents.  SFA have now delivered back the findings which will prioritise our improvement activities in this area going forward.","Upskilling our supply chain partners knowledge and understanding of Modern Slavery, Forced Labour and Human Rights.",Within your supply chains,Tier 1 suppliers,"Women
Migrants
Refugees",,United Kingdom,"Together with the United Nations Global Compact (UNGC) UK Network, we successfully completed a second consecutive year of the Sustainable Supplier Training programme. The programme delivered over 6 months included training via online content sessions with associated assessment quizzes and live webinars from both Stagecoach and the UNGC.",Enhancing our tender process due diligence specifically for sourcing our driver uniforms.,Within your supply chains,"Tier 1 suppliers
Tier 2 suppliers","Women
Migrants
Refugees
Children",,"Bangladesh
China
Cape Verde
United Kingdom
Indonesia
India
Sri Lanka
Mexico","With the guidance of Slave Free Alliance, we collaborated to design and implement a bespoke audit process, enhancing tender due diligence for supply chain partners operating in high-risk commodities and services.  Designed initially for our Uniform tender and involved a deeper review of our potential supplier partners supply chains for manufacture of the garments, we enhanced the obligations in our ITT docs, strengthened our MSA clauses and process for ongoing contract & supplier management.",,Yes,,,This year we have brokered a partnership with Slave Free Alliance and started a gap analysis programme.  This will report on areas we are managing well as an organisation and identify areas we have opportunity to improve on.  This will generate a plan for us to work towards and monitoring success against that plan will be part of the process.,2026-10-23T10:05:38,https://downloads.modern-slavery-statement-registry.service.gov.uk/pdf-published/EEMzaqq6/2026/Stagecoach Modern Slavery Statement - Sep 26.pdf
