Turkey","We commit to enhance our gender responsive approach to human rights due diligence. We joined the ETI community of practice to tackle gender-based violence and harassment (GBVH) in our supply chain. This work focused on identifying, preventing and mitigating and accounting for the risks of GBVH in supply chains using a gender responsive approach to human rights due diligence. We identified areas for improvement, refined our supply chain mapping and analysis of gender disaggregated data.","Workers affected by State Imposed Forced labour in specific geographies, to include China. Specific concerns looks at the impact of SILF on labour transfer of workers from the XUAR to Mainland China.",Within your supply chains,"Tier 1 suppliers
Tier 2 suppliers
Tier 3 suppliers and below","Women
Migrants
Children",,China,"Large evidence demonstrated presence of the direct and indirect links between global supply chains and the use of a workforce forced to work by China under repressive policies. SILF has become an areas of concern, and as such we have taken steps to mitigate this. We have worked with expert organisations like the Global Rights Compliance to develop and broaden our understanding of the context of SILF in global supply chains.","Informal workers in the homeworking economy, specifically in geographies such as rural India.",Within your supply chains,"Tier 1 suppliers
Tier 2 suppliers
Tier 3 suppliers and below",Women,,India,"We welcome the presence of homeworkers in the supply chain but recognises that working conditions can be poor with limited visibility. Our focus is on ensuring workers are part of our global risk assessment, and reviewing our policy. We increased our understanding of the prevalence and nature of homeworking risks and are looking at prioritising follow-up activities. This will be contextualising risks such as working countries, drilling down on product risks, supplier risks.",,Yes,,,We have set progress goals for our next statement and are currently working on setting measurable KPIs too.,2026-10-28T16:30:28,https://downloads.modern-slavery-statement-registry.service.gov.uk/pdf-published/AEJkedkS/2026/FY2026 TFG Brands (London) Ltd - Transparency Statement.pdf
