Working with modern slavery charity A21, LBA has introduced signage across the airport, increasing awareness of modern slavery and how to report any concerns.",There is a risk that members of our supplier workforce may be the victim of modern slavery.,Within your supply chains,Don't know,Migrants,,United Kingdom,"Our supplier agreement templates & tenders include modern slavery and human trafficking warranties and undertakings, and we reserve the right to terminate our commercial partnership with any supplier who is found to be in breach of, or who fails to comply with the Act. We also have a Supplier Code of Conduct which states our suppliers “must have zero tolerance of modern slavery and human trafficking and ensure that no form of modern slavery or human trafficking exists within their supply chain.",There is a risk our staff may be required to deal with victims of modern slavery in the workplace,Within your own operations,,"Women
Migrants
Refugees
Children
Other vulnerable groups",Men,,"All staff are required to undertake modern slavery training to increase awareness and understanding. A21 has provided additional training to frontline staff to reinforce the mandatory e-learning training, and rolled out informative posters which include a hotline to report suspicions. LBA also engage with West Yorkshire Police to explore additional ways of supporting employees when dealing with modern slavery concerns.",,Yes,,,"We use the following KPIs to measure performance: 
1. The number of instances of modern slavery and human trafficking identified as part of our supplier due diligence process. 
2. The number of instances of reports being received from employees, the public or law enforcement agencies that modern slavery and human trafficking practices have been identified within the 
Group. 
3. Monitoring percentage of completed e-learning modules. 

